<title>FRANCE: EU sets negative corrective on August grain export.</title>
<headline>EU sets negative corrective on August grain export.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union has set a negative corrective of 10 Ecus per tonne on refunds for grain exports in August, grain industry sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The corrective will apply to grain export licences awarded by the EU as of April 1 on a daily basis and through the weekly grain auction channel, they said.</p>
<p>Grain export licences are valid for the current month plus four months.</p>
<p>Since March 1 the same negative corrective of 10 Ecus per tonne has applied to refunds for the export of grain during the month of July.</p>
<p>The EU held at zero the corrective applying to grain exports between April 1 and June 30, sources said.</p>
<p>Negative correctives are set to restrict grain exports when the new campaign starts on July 1.</p>
</text>
